1
00:00:00,483 --> 00:00:01,810
Last video ended here.

2
00:00:02,394 --> 00:00:05,687
This snapper is forty-five centimetres, five above the

3
00:00:05,847 --> 00:00:07,153
average snapper off this jetty.

4
00:00:07,756 --> 00:00:10,949
This golden perch is forty centimetres, four above

5
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:12,556
the average perch in its river.

6
00:00:13,282 --> 00:00:14,533
Five looks bigger than four.

7
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:17,821
But snapper here vary by about four centimetres,

8
00:00:18,222 --> 00:00:19,863
and these perch by only about two and

9
00:00:19,904 --> 00:00:22,384
a half, so the raw gaps can't be

10
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:22,845
compared.

11
00:00:23,609 --> 00:00:25,014
We need a common ruler.

12
00:00:25,719 --> 00:00:27,933
Then we'll find the area beyond each catch.

13
00:00:29,175 --> 00:00:31,042
The ruler is the standard deviation.

14
00:00:31,766 --> 00:00:33,548
For the snapper, sigma is four,

15
00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:37,254
so five centimetres is five over four, one

16
00:00:37,295 --> 00:00:38,416
point two five sigmas.

17
00:00:39,359 --> 00:00:41,822
For the perch, sigma is two point five,

18
00:00:42,283 --> 00:00:44,846
so four centimetres is four over two point

19
00:00:44,907 --> 00:00:45,227
five,

20
00:00:45,789 --> 00:00:46,990
one point six sigmas.

21
00:00:48,013 --> 00:00:51,109
That count is the zed score, or standardised

22
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:51,431
score.

23
00:00:52,095 --> 00:00:54,446
Subtract the mean from the value, then divide

24
00:00:54,487 --> 00:00:55,732
by the standard deviation.

25
00:00:56,376 --> 00:00:58,681
It tells you how many standard deviations the

26
00:00:58,722 --> 00:01:00,727
value lies above or below the mean.

27
00:01:01,571 --> 00:01:03,158
A negative zed means below,

28
00:01:03,802 --> 00:01:04,887
positive means above.

29
00:01:05,671 --> 00:01:06,854
Both catches are above,

30
00:01:07,357 --> 00:01:09,263
and the perch is further out, because one

31
00:01:09,304 --> 00:01:11,450
point six sigmas is more than one point

32
00:01:11,511 --> 00:01:11,992
two five.

33
00:01:12,701 --> 00:01:14,327
Here's what a zed score does to the

34
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:15,109
whole curve.

35
00:01:15,651 --> 00:01:17,857
Subtracting the mean slides the bell so its

36
00:01:17,898 --> 00:01:19,041
centre sits at zero.

37
00:01:19,624 --> 00:01:22,512
Dividing by sigma squeezes it until its standard

38
00:01:22,532 --> 00:01:23,716
deviation is one.

39
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:26,409
Do that to both bells, and they land

40
00:01:26,509 --> 00:01:27,514
on the same curve.

41
00:01:28,137 --> 00:01:31,281
It's the standard normal distribution, with mean zero

42
00:01:31,523 --> 00:01:33,124
and standard deviation one,

43
00:01:33,646 --> 00:01:36,530
written capital Z is N of zero, one.

44
00:01:37,594 --> 00:01:40,018
Any other normal, with mean mu and standard

45
00:01:40,039 --> 00:01:43,004
deviation sigma, is a non-standard normal.

46
00:01:43,807 --> 00:01:46,192
The value marks move with the curve, so

47
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:47,455
the areas don't change.

48
00:01:48,138 --> 00:01:50,949
The area beyond forty-five centimetres is the area

49
00:01:51,031 --> 00:01:52,677
beyond one point two five.

50
00:01:53,448 --> 00:01:56,336
Zed scores also compare results from different groups.

51
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:59,809
Alex scored seventy-two in Maths, where the mean

52
00:01:59,831 --> 00:02:02,179
was sixty and the standard deviation twelve.

53
00:02:02,902 --> 00:02:06,929
Blake scored sixty-eight in English, with mean fifty-five

54
00:02:07,091 --> 00:02:08,472
and standard deviation ten.

55
00:02:09,518 --> 00:02:10,792
Alex has the higher mark.

56
00:02:11,258 --> 00:02:13,891
But Alex's zed score is twelve over twelve,

57
00:02:14,094 --> 00:02:14,636
which is one.

58
00:02:15,542 --> 00:02:18,336
Blake's is thirteen over ten, one point three.

59
00:02:19,061 --> 00:02:21,545
So Blake did better relative to the cohort,

60
00:02:21,806 --> 00:02:24,169
because Blake's mark is further above its mean,

61
00:02:24,451 --> 00:02:26,013
measured in standard deviations.

62
00:02:26,695 --> 00:02:29,485
To justify a comparison, quote both zed scores.

63
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,160
Now the areas.

64
00:02:31,928 --> 00:02:35,500
Every normal curve becomes the same standard normal,

65
00:02:35,521 --> 00:02:37,227
so one table works for all of them.

66
00:02:37,890 --> 00:02:40,214
This table gives the probability that Z is

67
00:02:40,275 --> 00:02:42,518
less than zed, the area to the left,

68
00:02:42,819 --> 00:02:43,780
for positive zeds.

69
00:02:44,563 --> 00:02:46,849
For one point two five, go down to

70
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:49,056
the row for one point two, then across

71
00:02:49,077 --> 00:02:51,223
to the column for zero point zero five.

72
00:02:51,846 --> 00:02:54,300
The entry is zero point eight nine four

73
00:02:54,342 --> 00:02:54,562
four.

74
00:02:55,166 --> 00:02:56,409
That's the area to the left,

75
00:02:56,931 --> 00:02:59,537
so the area beyond the snapper is one

76
00:02:59,759 --> 00:03:00,340
minus that,

77
00:03:00,982 --> 00:03:02,846
zero point one zero five six.

78
00:03:03,569 --> 00:03:05,892
At one point six, the table gives zero

79
00:03:05,953 --> 00:03:07,394
point nine four five two,

80
00:03:07,976 --> 00:03:10,259
so beyond the perch is zero point zero

81
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:11,220
five four eight.

82
00:03:12,043 --> 00:03:14,786
Under these normal models, about one snapper in

83
00:03:14,847 --> 00:03:17,391
ten is at least that long, but only

84
00:03:17,452 --> 00:03:18,773
about one perch in eighteen.

85
00:03:19,536 --> 00:03:22,181
Further out means a smaller tail, so the

86
00:03:22,222 --> 00:03:24,125
perch is the more unusual catch.

87
00:03:24,808 --> 00:03:28,115
This table has no negative zeds, and symmetry

88
00:03:28,176 --> 00:03:28,676
fixes that.

89
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:32,231
A drink-bottle filling machine aims for five hundred

90
00:03:32,273 --> 00:03:33,919
millilitres, with sigma eight.

91
00:03:34,643 --> 00:03:37,072
A bottle with four ninety is ten below,

92
00:03:37,494 --> 00:03:39,942
so zed is minus one point two five.

93
00:03:40,706 --> 00:03:42,910
The area below minus one point two five

94
00:03:43,352 --> 00:03:45,936
matches the area above plus one point two

95
00:03:45,977 --> 00:03:47,359
five, the snapper's tail.

96
00:03:47,921 --> 00:03:50,505
So it's zero point one zero five six,

97
00:03:51,007 --> 00:03:53,069
and about ten point six percent of bottles

98
00:03:53,151 --> 00:03:54,492
fall below four ninety.

99
00:03:55,295 --> 00:03:57,579
Any negative zed works the same way: flip

100
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,624
to the other side, then take one minus

101
00:03:59,645 --> 00:04:00,005
the table.

102
00:04:00,709 --> 00:04:02,496
For a middle, use symmetry again.

103
00:04:03,219 --> 00:04:05,523
Bolts are normal, with mean fifty millimetres and

104
00:04:05,584 --> 00:04:08,409
standard deviation zero point three, and pass between

105
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:10,613
forty-nine point five and fifty point five.

106
00:04:11,355 --> 00:04:13,118
Zed is plus or minus one point six

107
00:04:13,159 --> 00:04:15,542
seven, so each tail is one minus zero

108
00:04:15,583 --> 00:04:17,807
point nine five two five, which is zero

109
00:04:17,868 --> 00:04:19,229
point zero four seven five.

110
00:04:19,952 --> 00:04:22,385
The middle is one minus both tails, about

111
00:04:22,486 --> 00:04:23,793
zero point nine zero five.

112
00:04:24,196 --> 00:04:26,243
So about ninety point five percent of bolts

113
00:04:26,284 --> 00:04:26,524
pass.

114
00:04:27,322 --> 00:04:29,271
Zed scores also support judgements.

115
00:04:29,894 --> 00:04:31,925
A quality check finds a bottle holding four

116
00:04:31,985 --> 00:04:33,011
seventy-four millilitres.

117
00:04:33,675 --> 00:04:36,206
Its zed score is minus twenty-six over eight,

118
00:04:36,588 --> 00:04:38,275
which is minus three point two five.

119
00:04:39,058 --> 00:04:41,360
The table gives zero point nine nine nine

120
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:44,202
four at three point two five, so the

121
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:46,963
tail below is about zero point zero zero

122
00:04:46,983 --> 00:04:47,624
zero six.

123
00:04:48,326 --> 00:04:50,029
If the machine is still working as modelled,

124
00:04:50,471 --> 00:04:52,816
only about six bottles in ten thousand would

125
00:04:52,837 --> 00:04:53,317
be that low.

126
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,752
So finding one is a good reason to

127
00:04:55,794 --> 00:04:56,397
check the machine.

128
00:04:57,122 --> 00:04:58,549
Here's a way to remember the table.

129
00:04:59,474 --> 00:05:01,054
This table looks left.

130
00:05:01,719 --> 00:05:04,211
For a right tail, take one minus.

131
00:05:04,913 --> 00:05:07,338
For a negative zed, use the mirror tail

132
00:05:07,538 --> 00:05:08,279
on the other side.

133
00:05:11,078 --> 00:05:11,502
Your turn.

134
00:05:11,968 --> 00:05:13,232
Compare the two results.

135
00:05:14,018 --> 00:05:15,149
Pause here to answer.

136
00:05:25,861 --> 00:05:29,816
In English, zed is seventy-four minus sixty-two, over

137
00:05:29,936 --> 00:05:31,723
eight, which is one point five.

138
00:05:32,566 --> 00:05:36,014
In Maths, zed is eighty-one minus seventy, over

139
00:05:36,074 --> 00:05:37,397
ten, which is one point one.

140
00:05:38,901 --> 00:05:41,331
One point five is bigger, so Priya did

141
00:05:41,412 --> 00:05:43,741
better in English, relative to the cohort.

142
00:05:44,526 --> 00:05:47,174
Choosing Maths because eighty-one is the higher mark

143
00:05:47,376 --> 00:05:47,776
is wrong.

144
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:50,151
The two marks come from groups with different

145
00:05:50,232 --> 00:05:51,197
means and spreads.

146
00:05:52,998 --> 00:05:53,442
Last one.

147
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:55,624
Use the table values on the card.

148
00:05:55,947 --> 00:05:56,991
Pause here to answer.

149
00:06:07,648 --> 00:06:10,056
The variance is nine, so sigma is three.

150
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:14,107
Zed is forty-six point five minus forty-two, over

151
00:06:14,189 --> 00:06:16,233
three, which is one point five.

152
00:06:16,915 --> 00:06:18,978
The table gives zero point nine three three

153
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:21,223
two to the left, so the right tail

154
00:06:21,324 --> 00:06:24,088
is one minus that, zero point zero six

155
00:06:24,129 --> 00:06:24,709
six eight.

156
00:06:25,795 --> 00:06:27,652
A zed of zero point five is wrong.

157
00:06:28,076 --> 00:06:30,084
That divides by the variance, not by sigma.

158
00:06:31,774 --> 00:06:35,297
So a zed score counts standard deviations, compares

159
00:06:35,358 --> 00:06:38,100
results, and turns any normal area into a

160
00:06:38,161 --> 00:06:38,840
table look-up.

161
00:06:39,744 --> 00:06:41,553
Next, the question runs backwards.

162
00:06:42,216 --> 00:06:44,521
The company wants only one percent of bottles

163
00:06:44,602 --> 00:06:45,583
below four ninety,

164
00:06:46,266 --> 00:06:47,749
and sigma stays at eight.

165
00:06:48,615 --> 00:06:50,169
Where must it set the mean?

166
00:06:52,888 --> 00:06:53,771
Here are the key notes.

